  ('capability:mission_recommendation_bridge', 'check_business_priorities now returns a real missionRecommendation -- Priority Engine + Autonomy Decision Layer + Missions genuinely connected (master brief section 14)', 'Section 14 explicitly asks: "The Brain should be able to determine when a mission should be created." Investigated first: create_mission (packages/agent-core/src/tools/client/tools.ts, admin/mutation-tools.ts) already exists, already real, already confirm-gated (risk: external_mutation) -- mission creation itself was never the gap. The missing piece was connecting a real priority to a real governance decision about whether creating one makes sense. check_business_priorities (Update 38) now composes its own real topPriority bottleneck with decideAutonomyLevel (Update 39, the real autonomy decision layer) -- severity maps to riskLevel, the bottleneck''s own real confidence passes straight through, reversible is true (missions are cancellable via mission:cancel), no cost estimate is invented (honestly omitted, unknown at this stage). Returns { suggestedGoalText, decision: { level, reasonCode, humanReason } }. Purely advisory: never calls create_mission itself, never creates anything -- a human or a subsequent agent turn still has to explicitly call create_mission with the suggested goalText, same as every other advisory tool this session built.', 'ecosystem', null, 'check_business_priorities', 'lib/agent-core/business-priorities-tool.ts', 'Engineering', null, 'agent:read:research', 'read', 'tenant', 'free', 'read', 'The underlying decideAutonomyLevel is already covered by autonomy-decision.test.ts (13 assertions); this addition is thin composition/wiring within the existing tool, verified via full-repo tsc --noEmit clean, lint clean, real NODE_ENV=production next build exit 0 -- matching the established verification depth for every other AgentTool file in this session with no dedicated mocked test (autonomy-decision-tool.ts, google-business-tool.ts).', 